Directory streams of a 64 MiB disk written for these tests on Linux
(mkfs.fat, mkfs.exfat, then mounted, `tz=UTC` for FAT): the same small tree
on a FAT32, a FAT16 and an exFAT partition, files given known modification
and access times with touch, a file deleted. Each file is one directory's
entries as sootmark-intake lists them from the image:

  fat32-root.bin      vol0/$FAT_DIRECTORY
  fat32-folder-a.bin  vol0/Folder A/$FAT_DIRECTORY
  exfat-root.bin      vol2/$EXFAT_DIRECTORY

The Sleuth Kit 4.12.1 (`fls -r -m / -z UTC`) lists the same entries with
the same sizes and times, to the second. Under this crate's licences.
